These coupled ordinary differential equations describe the evolution of the concentrations \([H](t),[C](t),[S](t)\) during the linear temperature ramp (heating and cooling), with the explicit temperature dependence of each rate constant introduced through the ramp rate \(\beta\) via \(T(t)=T_{0}\pm\beta t\).

