\[
\begin{aligned}
\textbf{Harmonic fit:}&\qquad 
V_{\rm harm}(q)=\tfrac12\,k\,q^{2}
\;\Longrightarrow\;
k \;=\;2\,c_{2}
\;=\;\left.\frac{{\rm d}^{2}E}{{\rm d}q^{2}}\right|_{q=0},
\end{aligned}
\]

where \(c_{2}\) is the coefficient of the \(q^{2}\) term obtained from the quadratic fit (or the fitted parameter \(k\) itself).

\[
\begin{aligned}
\textbf{Morse fit:}&\qquad 
V_{\rm Morse}(q)=D_{e}\bigl[1-e^{-a q}\bigr]^{2} .
\end{aligned}
\]

Expanding about the minimum (\(q=0\)) gives  

\[
V_{\rm Morse}(q)=D_{e}a^{2}q^{2}
- D_{e}a^{3}q^{3}
+\frac{7}{12}D_{e}a^{4}q^{4}+ \cdots .
\]

Comparing with the quartic force‑field expansion  

\[
V(q)=\tfrac12k\,q^{2}+\tfrac13k^{(3)}q^{3}+\tfrac14k^{(4)}q^{4},
\]

yields the relations  

\[
k = 2D_{e}a^{2},\qquad 
k^{(3)} = -3D_{e}a^{3},\qquad 
k^{(4)} = \frac{7}{3}D_{e}a^{4}.
\]

Hence the Morse parameters can be expressed through the fitted force‑constant coefficients as  

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
a &= -\frac{2}{3}\,\frac{k^{(3)}}{k}
    \;=\;\sqrt{\frac{6\,k^{(4)}}{7\,k}},\\[4pt]
D_{e} &= \frac{k}{2a^{2}}
      \;=\;\frac{9}{8}\,\frac{k^{3}}{k^{(3)2}}
      \;=\;\frac{7}{12}\,\frac{k^{2}}{k^{(4)}} .
\end{aligned}
}
\]

If the Morse potential is fitted directly, the fitted parameters themselves give \(D_{e}\) and \(a\); the above formulas provide the connection to the harmonic force constant and the cubic/quartic coefficients obtained from the polynomial fit.

\[
\boxed{\begin{aligned}
&\text{Morse potential:}\;V(q)=D_e\bigl[1-e^{-aq}\bigr]^2
      =\tfrac12kq^{2}+\tfrac13k^{(3)}q^{3}+\tfrac14k^{(4)}q^{4}+\cdots\\[2mm]
&\Rightarrow\;k=2D_ea^{2},\qquad 
   k^{(3)}=-3D_ea^{3},\qquad 
   k^{(4)}=\frac{7}{3}D_ea^{4},\\[2mm]
&\text{harmonic frequency } \omega_L=\sqrt{k}=a\sqrt{2D_e}.\\[2mm]
&\text{For a one–dimensional oscillator the VPT2 fundamental is }\\
&\qquad\nu_L^{\rm VPT2}
   =\omega_L+\frac{3k^{(4)}}{4\omega_L^{2}}
          -\frac{5\bigl(k^{(3)}\bigr)^{2}}{6\omega_L^{4}}\\[2mm]
&\qquad\;=\;a\sqrt{2D_e}
   +\frac{7D_ea^{4}}{4\omega_L^{2}}
   -\frac{15D_e^{2}a^{6}}{2\omega_L^{4}}\\[2mm]
&\qquad\;=\;a\sqrt{2D_e}-a^{2}
   \;=\;\omega_L-\frac{\omega_L^{2}}{2D_e}.\\[2mm]
&\text{Using the anharmonic constant }x_e=\frac{\omega_L}{4D_e},
   \;\;\frac{\omega_L^{2}}{2D_e}=2\omega_Lx_e,\\[2mm]
&\therefore\;\nu_L^{\rm VPT2}
   =\omega_L\Bigl(1-\frac{\omega_L}{2D_e}\Bigr)
   =\omega_L\bigl(1-2x_e\bigr)
   =\omega_L-2\omega_Lx_e+O(x_e^{2}) .
\end{aligned}}
\]

