**Derivation**

1. **Oxide‐inclusion fraction**  

\[
f_{\rm ox}=K_{\rm ox}\,\frac{[O]}{[Ti]+[O]}\qquad\text{(1)}
\]

For the reference heat (heat 1) the oxide fraction is  

\[
f_{\rm ox}^{\rm ref}=K_{\rm ox}\,\frac{[O]_{\rm ref}}{[Ti]_{\rm ref}+[O]_{\rm ref}}\qquad\text{(2)}
\]

2. **Inclusion size from the nucleation‑growth model**  

\[
d=d_{0}\Bigl(\frac{f_{\rm ox}}{f_{\rm ox}^{\rm ref}}\Bigr)^{\alpha}\qquad\text{(3)}
\]

Insert (1) and (2) into (3):

\[
\begin{aligned}
d&=d_{0}\Biggl[\frac{K_{\rm ox}\dfrac{[O]}{[Ti]+[O]}}{K_{\rm ox}\dfrac{[O]_{\rm ref}}{[Ti]_{\rm ref}+[O]_{\rm ref}}}\Biggr]^{\alpha}\\[4pt]
&=d_{0}\Biggl[\frac{[O]}{[Ti]+[O]}\,
\frac{[Ti]_{\rm ref}+[O]_{\rm ref}}{[O]_{\rm ref}}\Biggr]^{\alpha}\\[4pt]
&=d_{0}\Biggl[\frac{[O]\;\bigl([Ti]_{\rm ref}+[O]_{\rm ref}\bigr)}
{[O]_{\rm ref}\;\bigl([Ti]+[O]\bigr)}\Biggr]^{\alpha}\qquad\text{(4)}
\end{aligned}
\]

(If one prefers to keep the reference fraction as a single constant, (4) can be written as  
\(d=d_{0}\bigl[(K_{\rm ox}[O])/(([Ti]+[O])\,f_{\rm ox}^{\rm ref})\bigr]^{\alpha}\).)

3. **Fatigue‑limit relationship**  

\[
\sigma_{f}= \sigma_{0}\,\exp\!\Bigl(-\beta\,\frac{d}{d_{\rm crit}}\Bigr)\qquad\text{(5)}
\]

Substituting (4) into (5) gives the fatigue limit directly as a function of the measured O and Ti concentrations:

\[
\boxed{\;
\sigma_{f}= \sigma_{0}\,
\exp\!\Biggl[
-\frac{\beta\,d_{0}}{d_{\rm crit}}\,
\Biggl(\frac{[O]\;\bigl([Ti]_{\rm ref}+[O]_{\rm ref}\bigr)}
{[O]_{\rm ref}\;\bigl([Ti]+[O]\bigr)}\Biggr)^{\!\alpha}
\Biggr]\;
}
\]

or, using the compact notation with the reference oxide fraction,

\[
\boxed{\;
\sigma_{f}= \sigma_{0}\,
\exp\!\Biggl[
-\frac{\beta\,d_{0}}{d_{\rm crit}}\,
\Biggl(\frac{K_{\rm ox}[O]}{([Ti]+[O])\,f_{\rm ox}^{\rm ref}}\Biggr)^{\!\alpha}
\Biggr]\;
}
\]

Both forms express the fatigue limit \(\sigma_f\) explicitly in terms of the measured oxygen \([O]\) and titanium \([Ti]\) concentrations and the material constants \(K_{\rm ox}, d_{0}, \alpha, \sigma_{0}, \beta, d_{\rm crit}\).

