      {k_{0}^{\rm C\!-\!C}\,10^{\rho_{\rm C\!-\!C}\,\sigma}
      +k_{0}^{\rm C\!-\!O}\,10^{\rho_{\rm C\!-\!O}\,\sigma}}
\end{aligned}}
\]

where  

- \(k_{\rm OA}\) is the rate constant for the oxidative‑addition step (first‑order in catalyst and substrate),  
- \(k_{0}^{\rm C\!-\!C}\) and \(k_{0}^{\rm C\!-\!O}\) are the intrinsic (σ‑independent) rate constants for the C–C and C–O reductive‑elimination steps, respectively,  
- \(\sigma\) is the Hammett substituent constant for the combined 2‑, 4‑, and 6‑substituents on the aryl ring, and  
- \(\rho_{\rm C\!-\!C}\) and \(\rho_{\rm C\!-\!O}\) are the Hammett reaction constants that quantify how the substituents affect the C–C and C–O reductive‑elimination barriers.  (The ligand dependence is contained in the pre‑exponential factors \(k_{0}^{\rm C\!-\!C}\) and \(k_{0}^{\rm C\!-\!O}\).)

